    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **68 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field following the repo's existing conventions for derived owner fields.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema, typed as a string enum with the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` from this.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` plus a `deriveOwnerSegment(Owner)` helper that:\n- Derives **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(membershipPoints(owner)) >= 3`, else `STANDARD` \u2014 reusing the existing membership logic.\n- Derives **AREA** = `METRO` when `deriveLocality(owner)` is one of `NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, else `REGIONAL` \u2014 reusing the existing locality derivation.\n- Combines them as `<TIER>_<AREA>` via `OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(...)`.\n\nThis composes on the already-implemented `membershipLevel` and `locality` derivations rather than duplicating that logic, matching the surrounding code's style.",
